# XI Model Viewer — machine-specific paths.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and uncomment what you need:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Every value below is optional. A commented-out (or blank) entry keeps the
# built-in default shown next to it. A real environment variable always beats
# the .env file, so a one-off still works:
#     XI_GAME_DIR="$HOME/FFXI" ./start.sh
#
# Loaded by ./start.sh, ./build.sh, the Tauri app, dev/serve.py, and vite.config.js.
# Set XI_ENV_FILE to read a different file instead of this repo's `.env`; the
# app also falls back to a `.env` sitting next to the binary, for launches where
# the working directory isn't the repo (Finder, a desktop shortcut).

# FFXI install directory — the folder containing ROM/, ROM2/, FFXiMain.dll.
# Supplies the *default* only: a game path already saved in Settings
# (localStorage.gamePath) still wins.
# Default: C:\Program Files (x86)\PlayOnline\SquareEnix\FINAL FANTASY XI
#XI_GAME_DIR=/Users/you/FFXI

# vgmstream-cli, used to decode .bgw/.spw audio (ATRAC3).
# The copy bundled in src-tauri/vgmstream is a Windows build, so on macOS/Linux
# install it (brew install vgmstream) and point here if it isn't on PATH.
# Default: co-located vgmstream/ -> embedded copy (Windows) -> PATH
#XI_VGMSTREAM=/opt/homebrew/bin/vgmstream-cli

# xi-tools checkout (or xi.exe). Settings "xi-tools folder" wins over this.
# Repo folder is fine — looks in .venv/Scripts (or .venv/bin). Needs Python 3.14.
# Default: PATH -> ~/.local/bin/xi
#XI_CLI=D:/xi-tools

# Where the embedded vgmstream is unpacked on first use.
# Default: %LOCALAPPDATA% -> $XDG_CACHE_HOME -> ~/.cache -> system temp,
#          each + /XiModelViewer/vgmstream
#XI_CACHE_DIR=/Users/you/.cache

# dev/serve.py (browser dev mode, no Tauri). A port passed on the command line
# still beats XI_DEV_PORT.
# Defaults: 127.0.0.1 / 8766
#XI_DEV_HOST=127.0.0.1
#XI_DEV_PORT=8766

# Where Vite proxies /fs in browser dev mode — must match the serve.py address.
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:8766
#XI_FS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8766

# Where the app keeps its own data: the managed xi-tools checkout and caches.
# Default: %LOCALAPPDATA% (or ~/.local/share) + /XiModelViewer
#XI_DATA_DIR=D:/xi-model-viewer-data

# An xi-tools checkout to use as-is instead of the managed clone. Skips the
# clone/update step entirely, so the folder is yours to keep current.
# Default: a managed clone under XI_DATA_DIR
#XI_TOOLS_DIR=D:/xi-tools
